Article 4 (Principles in Accounting of Telecommunications Business)
Accounts of telecommunications business shall be settled in accordance with the following principles:
The outcomes of settlement of accounts shall be presented in a reliable, fair, and reasonable manner, and accounting records shall be maintained so that all outcomes can be objectively verified;
A method shall apply consistently to the settlement of accounts, and shall not be altered at random;
Except as otherwise provided for in this Decree, accounting standards generally accepted as fair and reasonable shall apply to the settlement of accounts.
The Minister of Science and ICT may prescribe and publicly notify more detailed rules necessary for the settlement of accounts of telecommunications business. <Amended by Presidential Decree No. 24445, Mar. 23, 2013; Presidential Decree No. 28210, Jul. 26, 2017>

