Article 7 (Tangible and Intangible Assets for Telecommunication Business)
Tangible assets for telecommunications business are as follows:
Telecommunications systems that directly form a telecommunications network;
General support assets that do not directly form a telecommunications network, but support such network, assets in transit, or assets under construction.
Intangible assets for telecommunications business shall be defined as intangible assets acquired in relation to telecommunications business.
The tangible and intangible assets for telecommunications business under paragraphs (1) and (2) (hereafter referred to as "tangible and intangible assets" in this paragraph) shall be classified as follows:
Tangible and intangible assets in use for telecommunications business: Assets not classifiable into those under subparagraph 2;
Tangible and intangible assets not in use for telecommunications business:
(a)Assets that have not been used for more than two years since they were acquired or completely constructed;
(b)Tangible and intangible assets that were used in the past for telecommunications business, but have not been used for more than two years.

