Article 9 (Classification of General Support Assets in Use)
The general support assets in use for telecommunications business shall be classified into the following categories: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
Land: Building sites, forests, fields, paddies, miscellaneous land, etc.;
Building: Buildings, facilities for cooling and heating, lighting fixtures, facilities for ventilation, power source equipment not for telecommunications, and other facilities annexed to buildings;
Structure: Docks, bridges, quays (quay walls), floating bridges (referring to bridges that float on water without supporting pillars), tracks, water reservoirs, mine shafts, chimneys, gardening facilities, and other civil engineering facilities or structures;
Ships: Ships and other water transportation means;
Vehicles: Railway vehicles, motor vehicles, and other land transportation means;
Other general support assets: General support assets not classifiable into any category of subparagraphs 1 through 5.

